From 107ea94b052f39cdaca2239aacfa01726a1870e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:49:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Phase 1: multi-tenant core, CRM, and AI Command Center
 foundation

Adds the tenant-isolated foundation for the AI Growth Operating System
alongside the existing single-tenant console (no existing table, policy,
page or route behaviour is removed).

Database (supabase/migrations/20261006120000_phase1_tenancy_crm_ai.sql)
- organizations (agency -> client sub-accounts), locations, memberships
  with an owner/admin/manager/member/viewer ladder enforced by RLS on
  auth.uid(); suspended orgs are read-only, closed orgs inaccessible
- unified CRM: companies, contacts, pipelines/stages, opportunities,
  tasks, custom field definitions, append-only consent history and an
  activity timeline (customer memory)
- composite (id, organization_id) foreign keys so rows cannot link
  across tenants
- AI Command Center: per-category AI policies (observe / recommend /
  ask approval / act automatically), conversations, and ai_actions with a
  database-enforced state machine; execution runs with the approving
  human's own rights
- append-only audit log, contact erasure, idempotent legacy import
- 54 SQL security tests against a local Supabase stand-in
  (npm run test:db)

Application
- Supabase Auth sessions with refresh tokens; non-staff users are
  limited to tenant modules; passcode sessions keep legacy access only
- tenant route wrapper: auth, RBAC, Zod validation, same-origin check,
  safe error mapping
- provider-agnostic chat model interface with an OpenAI adapter
- AI operator engine with validated tools over the shared CRM service,
  explainable lead scoring, and a persistent per-user rate limit
- new pages: AI Command Center, CRM (contacts, drag-and-drop pipeline,
  tasks, contact timeline/consent/privacy), Organization
- 25 unit tests (npm test)

